WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.460
Are we watching a bromance unfold in real
time, or was there something else going on

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.281
between Pedro Pascal and Kieran Culkin?

00:00:07.281 --> 00:00:10.620
Here's why Pascal was slinging shade at Culkin
at the Emmys.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.490
Viewers of the 75th Primetime Emmy Awards
may have done a double-take when Pedro Pascal

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.850
showed up with his arm in a sling, but they
did a triple-take when he called out Kieran

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.720
Culkin completely out of the blue.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.300
Pascal took to the podium to present an award
and opened by saying:

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.289
"Before we get into the nominees for best
supporting actor in a drama series, I'd like

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:31.682
to take just a second and make this about
me.

00:00:31.682 --> 00:00:33.940
A lot of people have been asking about my
arm."

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.950
The broadcast censored the punchline of his
story, but the uncensored clip on YouTube

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.408
clarified what he said.

00:00:39.408 --> 00:00:40.800
Pascal continued:

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.370
"It's actually my shoulder, and I think this
is the perfect time to tell everyone that

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.940
Kieran Culkin beat the s— out of me."

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.390
Immediately after, the cameras treated viewers
to a close-up of a stone-faced Culkin staring

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.420
at Pascal.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:57.280
Audiences got a laugh, and a few seconds later
Culkin cracked a smile as well.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.140
Awards shows are full of friendly jabs between
actors, but still…what was that all about?

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.950
First of all, no — Culkin didn't really
beat up Pascal.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.979
At least, probably not.

00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:11.290
On January 7, the actor told reporters that
he'd accidentally fallen.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:14.070
His Emmys joke played out more like a bit
of joking revenge.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:19.280
At the 2024 Golden Globes, Pascal and Culkin
were both nominated for the Golden Globe for

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.930
best performance by an actor in a drama series
for their work on "The Last of Us" and "Succession."

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:28.689
Culkin won and took a jab of his own at Pascal
in his acceptance speech.

00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:29.460
He said:

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.110
"Thanks to 'Succession' I've been in here
a couple times.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.229
It's nice, but I sort of accepted I was never
going to be on the stage.

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:36.964
So this is a nice moment.

00:01:36.964 --> 00:01:38.220
Suck it, Pedro."

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.630
Even this wasn't the beginning of the friendly
sniping between the pair.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:45.720
It's merely the latest chapter in what's shaping
up to be an endearing bromance between two

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.479
of the hottest actors in Hollywood.

00:01:47.479 --> 00:01:52.829
In 2023, the actors sat side by side during
The Hollywood Reporter's roundtable discussion

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:58.210
along with Jeff Bridges, Evan Peters, Michael
Imperioli, and Damson Idris . Throughout,

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:03.490
he and Pascal demonstrated an easy chemistry
that at times resembled a seasoned comedy act.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:08.834
"Amazingly, it gave me the opportunity to
be able to go and do something else."

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:11.000
"That's good.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.190
Do you ever…"

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:16.530
It looks like the two have decided to continue
the fun and games throughout the awards season.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.260
Though Pascal once again lost out to Culkin
when they were up for the same award at the

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:24.430
Emmys, cameras captured the two meeting up
in a crowd at the afterparty, where they appeared

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:28.030
to be on perfectly good terms, laughing and
smiling for the cameras.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.550
One video posted to X showed Culkin reaching
up to pat Pascal on the right shoulder — his

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.550
injured one — leading Pascal to not-so-subtly
move the hand to his good shoulder.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.930
Fans have been loving the dynamic between
Pascal and Culkin the whole time.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:45.170
After Pascal's joke at the Emmys, fans took
to social media to share their love for the

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.351
duo's dynamic.

00:02:46.351 --> 00:02:47.580
One person wrote:

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:53.310
"The real winner is us witnessing the evolution
of the duo that is pedro pascal + kieran culkin."

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:58.693
Meanwhile, another person compared their dynamic
to some other fan-favorite celebrity friendships, writing,

00:02:58.693 --> 00:03:03.690
"Kieran Culkin &amp; Pedro Pascal are the new
Ryan Reynolds &amp; Hugh Jackman, The Rock &amp; Kevin

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.950
Hart, Ken Jeong &amp; Joel McHale."

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:10.099
Another X user expressed hope that the decision
makers in Hollywood were taking note of the

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:12.950
obvious chemistry between Pascal and Culkin.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.770
Finally, one user had just a single humble
request, writing:

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:21.390
"I wish every award season could include kieran
culkin and pedro pascal."

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:25.420
Whether they're winning trophies or just razzing
each other on stage, we too would like to

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.696
see more of Pedro Pascal and Kieran Culkin's
antics at future award shows.

